```svelte
<script lang="ts">
import { Input } from "#lib/components/ui/input/index.js";
import * as Field from "#lib/components/ui/field/index.js";
import { MapPin, Link2, Navigation } from "@lucide/svelte"; // maybe

interface DestinationField { ... } // typing remote form fields generically is awkward.
```

Typing: remote form fields have `.as("text")`, `.issues()`. A structural type:

```ts
type FieldControl = {
  as: (type: "text") => { name: string; [key: string]: unknown };
  issues: () => { message: string }[];
};
```

Hmm, `as("hidden", value)` variant has different signature. For our three text fields, `as("text")`. Let me define the prop as the remote form's `fields` subset:

```ts
interface Props {
  fields: {
    destination_name: TextField;
    destination_address: TextField;
    directions_url: TextField;
  };
  disabled?: boolean;
}
```

