The anti-slop rule dislikes the explicit open Record type. Use inference with `satisfies`:

```ts
const destinationIssueFields = {
	destinationName: "destination_name",
	destinationAddress: "destination_address",
	directionsUrl: "directions_url",
} satisfies Record<string, "destination_name" | "destination_address" | "directions_url">;
```

Then `destinationIssueFields[field]` — indexing a closed object type with string → TS error (no index signature). Hmm. Alternative: a lookup function:

```ts
const destinationFormField = (field: string) => {
	switch (field) {
		case "destinationName": return "destination_name" as const;
		case "destinationAddress": return "destination_address" as const;
		case "directionsUrl": return "directions_url" as const;
		default: return undefined;
	}
};
```

No assertion, no widening — a switch. Clean. Let me do that.

